  "description": "CR 613.7f turning face down restamps the permanent after a removal that had wiped its grant",
  "note": "Repeat Offender is the suspect, suspecting itself with its own {2}{B}: a real road to CR 701.60c's designation, where the Haskell test wrote it onto a Goblin Piker. Suspected is no ability of the card (CR 701.60b), so CR 708.2 leaves it alone and its grant carries the permanent's own timestamp into layer 6 (CR 613.7a); that grant is the one effect on the board whose order against Turn to Frog's removal a turning-over can move. Turn to Frog is a spell, so CR 613.7b stamps it as it resolves. bob's other Goblin Piker, never suspected, is the anti-vacuity leg: it blocks. Turn to Frog resolves after the suspect entered, so CR 613.1f wipes the grant; then Ixidron turns all other nontoken creatures face down as it enters, so its victims need no morph ability. Three go face down and it settles a 3/3; bob's lands stay face up. The sweep restamps the suspect after the removal, so menace is back and it can't block.",
